claimed: deploy-model -- stage 0, first half (specs/deployment.md): the model and the two targets that need no account. okay.deploy gains Deployment/Service/Run/Need/Settings/Health/Scale/Resources with derived Schemas (the CLI reads the value as JSON, so every node must round-trip), Settings.of[A] deriving environment names from a Schema, and two pure renderers -- `laptop` (compose.yaml: the service, its needs as containers, volumes, an .env.example) and `host` (a systemd unit per service, an EnvironmentFile, an install script) -- with Deployment.render/write/drift generalised over targets. Golden tests per target; the doctor, the CLI and the Live proofs are the second half. The existing single-service Deploy value keeps working: okay-script's ScriptDeploy is ported in the SAME landing so the model is proven on a real application, not a fixture.
